SAL-4082 / PR #115 — end-to-end demo  (passport 0.7.0, express-session, Salla endpoints stubbed)

FLOW 1 — PR #115 as written
   callback route: passport.authenticate("salla", {"failureRedirect":"/login"})

   → alice logs in via Salla OAuth ... HTTP 200 "logged in"
   → bob logs in via Salla OAuth ... HTTP 200 "logged in"

   → GET /orders as alice ... HTTP 200 {"user":"bob","orders":[{"order":"#1001","store":"bob"}]}
   → GET /orders as bob   ... HTTP 200 {"user":"bob","orders":[{"order":"#1001","store":"bob"}]}
   → GET /orders as anon  ... HTTP 200 {"user":"bob","orders":[{"order":"#1001","store":"bob"}]}

   ✘ FAIL alice cannot fetch her orders -> 200
   ✔ PASS bob gets HIS OWN orders
   ✘ FAIL anonymous visitor got access

   RESULT: BROKEN

FLOW 2 — PR #115 + proposed fix (keepSessionInfo: true)
   callback route: passport.authenticate("salla", {"failureRedirect":"/login","keepSessionInfo":true})

   → alice logs in via Salla OAuth ... HTTP 200 "logged in"
   → bob logs in via Salla OAuth ... HTTP 200 "logged in"

   → GET /orders as alice ... HTTP 200 {"user":"bob","orders":[{"order":"#1001","store":"bob"}]}
   → GET /orders as bob   ... HTTP 200 {"user":"bob","orders":[{"order":"#1001","store":"bob"}]}
   → GET /orders as anon  ... HTTP 200 {"user":"bob","orders":[{"order":"#1001","store":"bob"}]}

   ✘ FAIL alice cannot fetch her orders -> 200
   ✔ PASS bob gets HIS OWN orders
   ✘ FAIL anonymous visitor got access

   RESULT: BROKEN

SUMMARY
   Flow 1  PR #115 as written      : BROKEN — users log in but their Salla token is lost
   Flow 2  PR #115 + proposed fix  : BROKEN

